15
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:52,000
Silav û rêz ji şêniyên gundê Hec Xelîl re. Silavên me ji
were hene, hûn bi xêr hatin ser qenala Hatim li Efrîn.
 
Greetings and respect to the residents of Hec Xelîl village.
Our greetings to you, welcome to the channel Hatim li Efrîn.

16
00:01:52,000 --> 00:01:55,000
Gundê Hec Xelîl çiyayê Efrîn dikeve, li Rajo...
 
The village of Hec Xelîl is located in the Afrin mountain,
in Rajo...

17
00:01:55,000 --> 00:01:58,000
Îro emê mêvanê hevalê xwe bin û gelî têra jî cîranê xwe bin.
 
Today we will be guests of our friend and generally
neighbors.

18
00:01:58,000 --> 00:02:01,000
Ka nuhab me ra bin bi dilekî xweş û geş emê derbas gundê Hec
Xelîl bin, emê biçin...
 
So stay with us with a happy and bright heart, we will enter
the village of Hec Xelîl, we will go...

19
00:02:01,000 --> 00:02:05,000
Dîrokê vî gundî nas kin, emê adet û teqalîdê vî gundî nas
kin.
 
To get to know the history of this village, we will get to
know the customs and traditions of this village.

20
00:02:05,000 --> 00:02:22,000
Saeta we xweş û bi me ra bin heta toliya vîdyo.
 
Have a good time and stay with us until the end of the
video.

21
00:02:22,000 --> 00:02:23,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

22
00:02:23,000 --> 00:02:30,000
Ehlen wa sehlen, bi hatina we ya vê... şuxlî we ra... em bi
kêfxweş in şebabê wek we me ra werin, em gîş tînin...
 
Welcome, with your coming for this... work of yours... we
are happy that youth like you come to us, we welcome you
all...

23
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:37,000
Em bi vî rihî... em bibînin... şebabê me û karê xwe yî îlamî
xû di alemê da bela be... dûr û nêzîk me nas kin ortaq.
 
We, with this spirit... we see... our youth and their media
work spreading in the world... so far and near get to know
us, friend.

24
00:02:37,000 --> 00:02:38,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

25
00:02:38,000 --> 00:02:39,000
Ehlen wa sehlen.
 
Welcome.

26
00:02:39,000 --> 00:02:40,000
Navî te bi xêr?
 
Your name please?

27
00:02:40,000 --> 00:02:45,000
Navî min Hisên Henan Reşîd im ji gundê Hec Xelîl de me.
 
My name is Hisên Henan Reşîd, I am from the village of Hec
Xelîl.

28
00:02:45,000 --> 00:02:47,000
Bavê Elî me ez, ehlen wa sehlen.
 
I am Bavê Elî (Ali's Father), welcome.

29
00:02:47,000 --> 00:02:49,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

30
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:56,000
Bavê Elî ez Xelîl ji gundê Baedîna, ji qenala Hatim li
Efrîn, îro em mêvanê gundê Hec Xelîl in.
 
Bavê Elî, I am Khalil from the village of Baedîna, from the
channel Hatim li Efrîn, today we are guests of Hec Xelîl
village.

31
00:02:56,000 --> 00:03:02,000
Ehlen wa sehlen bi navî gundê Hec Xelîl û bi navî hatina cem
min û tû û cemeata xwe fersa ser serî min ser çavê min.
 
Welcome in the name of Hec Xelîl village and in the name of
coming to me, you and your group are welcome upon my head
and upon my eyes.

32
00:03:02,000 --> 00:03:10,000
Em kêfxweş in bi hatina we giya û her kesî karê kî însanî
bike... û alemê piçî tiştî nas ke, me pê nas ke em bi
kêfxweş in.
 
We are happy with all your coming and anyone who does a
humanitarian work... and lets the world know a little
something, gets to know us, we are happy.

33
00:03:10,000 --> 00:03:15,000
Em derbas gundê Hec Xelîl bûn, malê te pisilef em derbas
bûn, malê Bavê Elî cagh de.
 
We entered the village of Hec Xelîl, we stopped by your home
first, at Bavê Elî's house.

34
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:27,000
Tu çişkî ji me ra xeber de... wextê Hec Xelîl neçêbûye...
malbatên pisilef hatine kî bûn? Û emrê vî gundî dorê çiqas
sal e?
 
Tell us a little bit... when Hec Xelîl was not yet
established... who were the first families that came? And
how old is this village, around how many years?

35
00:03:27,000 --> 00:03:30,000
Û çişkî li ser gund ji me ra xeber de, melûmatê me de.
 
And tell us a little about the village, give us information.

36
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:35,000
Gundê Hec Xelîl emrê xwe dora 250 salî ye.
 
The village of Hec Xelîl is around 250 years old.

37
00:03:35,000 --> 00:03:40,000
Malbatên silef li vî gundî çêbûn, eylak tenê bûn... dibên
malê tetû...
 
The ancestral families established in this village, were a
single family... they say Mala Tetû...

38
00:03:40,000 --> 00:03:44,000
250 salî da ser erqekî dijişîn heta noka...
 
For 250 years they lived on a lineage until now...

39
00:03:44,000 --> 00:03:49,000
Em hatin bûn cîranê gund da, malbatek din hatin mala Hecû...
 
We came and became neighbors in the village, another family
came, Mala Hecû...

40
00:03:49,000 --> 00:03:54,000
Me cîranliq bi hevra kir û paşê re gund yavaş yavaş zêde
bûn.
 
We practiced neighborliness together and afterwards the
village slowly grew.

41
00:03:54,000 --> 00:04:00,000
Ayle didû li me çêbûn û Hec Xelîl bixwe... ê ji Hec Xelîl
bixwe, sê ayle bûn.
 
Two families were established with us and Hec Xelîl
itself... those from Hec Xelîl itself were three families.

42
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:06,000
Ayle mala Bilê... yan tami mala fir'ê Reşo ye Hec Xelîl em
dibêjin.
 
The family Mala Bilê... or the complete branch of Reşo of
Hec Xelîl we call them.

43
00:04:06,000 --> 00:04:14,000
Ayle mala Ehmed... aylekî Bekir... em dibêjin mala Bekû,
mala Ehmû, mala Reşo. Em hevbûn.
 
The family Mala Ehmed... the family of Bekir... We call them
Mala Bekû, Mala Ehmû, Mala Reşo. We were together.

44
00:04:14,000 --> 00:04:22,000
Wa keza... ji me zêde bûn mal pir bûn û cîranê me mala Hecû
hew jî pir bûn...
 
And so... we increased, the houses became many and our
neighbors Mala Hecû also became many...

45
00:04:22,000 --> 00:04:30,000
Ê cîranê din me re hatine... yavaş yavaş tev me bûn heta
noka bûne cîranliqî gund kirin malbatê gund.
 
The other neighbors who came to us... slowly joined us until
now they became the neighborhood of the village, they made
the families of the village.

46
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:38,000
Em ji evder ne dûr in e... em ne pir dûr bûn, em ne bi
qelş... xal û xwarzî evder ne.
 
We are not far from here... we were not very far, we are not
split... we are maternal uncles and nephews here.

47
00:04:38,000 --> 00:04:42,000
Em tev evder bûn û ji hev ra kindin... tiştin evder...
ewanan nîzîk bûn e.
 
We were all here and [related] to each other... things
here... those were close.

48
00:04:42,000 --> 00:04:44,000
Hemû nav gundî Hec Xelîl da tişta heye.
 
Everyone in the village of Hec Xelîl has this [connection].

49
00:04:44,000 --> 00:04:50,000
Bavê Elî niha xîn nav lê bî Hec Xelîl, yanî vê navê ji kî va
hat?
 
Bavê Elî, now the name became Hec Xelîl, meaning from whom
did this name come?

50
00:04:50,000 --> 00:04:55,000
Hec Xelîl hewa navê şexsekî bû, ji Xeyamê hat.
 
Hec Xelîl was the name of a person, he came from Xeyam.

51
00:04:55,000 --> 00:05:01,000
Pîşî gindê... hatin li gund... berê xirabe bû... dibû xirabê
malê filanî... filanî... li wir rûniştin.
 
Before the village... they came to the village... it was
ruins before... it was called the ruins of such and such
house... such and such... they settled there.

52
00:05:01,000 --> 00:05:04,000
Hewa Hec Xelîl ji Xeyamê hat.
 
That Hec Xelîl came from Xeyam.

53
00:05:04,000 --> 00:05:09,000
Hew birakî xwe va... didû... zaq û çûq hebûn... Elşêr hebû,
Memik hebû... em ji fir'ê malê Memik in e.
 
He and his brother... two... there were kids... there was
Elşêr, there was Memik... we are from the branch of Mala
Memik.

54
00:05:09,000 --> 00:05:14,000
Elşêr... hinek jê hat kuştin... tarîx dûr, em nakevin
tefasîlê na.
 
Elşêr... some of them were killed... history is long, we
won't go into details now.

55
00:05:14,000 --> 00:05:16,000
Hec Xelîl ji wir da hat.
 
Hec Xelîl came from there.

56
00:05:16,000 --> 00:05:18,000
Yanî manî nav lê kirin Hec Xelîl.
 
Meaning that's why they named it Hec Xelîl.

57
00:05:18,000 --> 00:05:20,000
Hec Xelîl... ji wir da hat. Belê tebeqan.
 
Hec Xelîl... came from there. Yes, absolutely.

58
00:05:20,000 --> 00:05:24,000
Hec Xelîl niha... em sar niha dên kin, dorê çiqas mal e?
 
Hec Xelîl now... if we look at it now, around how many
houses?

59
00:05:24,000 --> 00:05:28,000
Niha dora 240 malî heta 250 malî heye.
 
Now there are around 240 to 250 houses.

60
00:05:28,000 --> 00:05:30,000
Heta 250 malî heye.
 
Up to 250 houses.

61
00:05:30,000 --> 00:05:31,000
Êd gund da.
 
In the village.

62
00:05:31,000 --> 00:05:33,000
Êd gund da, yawa.
 
In the village, yes.

63
00:05:33,000 --> 00:05:40,000
Gundê Hec Xelîl bixwe li nahya Raco dikeve. Dorê çend
kîlometre ji nahyê xû dûr dikeve?
 
Hec Xelîl village itself falls in Rajo district. About how
many kilometers is it far from its district?

64
00:05:40,000 --> 00:05:43,000
Dorê du kîlo du sêsed metir ji şerqî Raco dikeve gundê Hec
Xelîl.
 
About two kilometers and two-three hundred meters east of
Rajo lies Hec Xelîl village.

65
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:45,000
Û ji Bilbilê va çiqas dûr dikeve?
 
And how far is it from Bilbile?

66
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:52,000
Ji Bilbilê va teqrîben... teke jê terh ke... Bilbil dem e sî
kîlometre ye... ji dused... bîst û pênc kîlometre dike behsa
Bilbil bi ma va dûr.
 
From Bilbile approximately... if you subtract a bit...
Bilbil is maybe 30 km... from two hundred... it makes 25 km,
Bilbil is relatively far from us.

67
00:05:52,000 --> 00:06:01,000
Niha berê... Bavê Elî... gûne tîgiştî ye, yanî berê da heye
niha gundê Hec Xelîl mîrkê vî gundî pir çi kar dikin... yan
bi çi va radibin?
 
Now before... Bavê Elî... generally speaking, meaning in the
past and now, what work do the people of this village mostly
do... or what do they engage in?

68
00:06:01,000 --> 00:06:08,000
Va gunda... destpêkê em giş rencber û cûtkir bûn.
 
This village... in the beginning we were all laborers and
farmers.

69
00:06:08,000 --> 00:06:16,000
Û fîa gundî me hebi tebeqak hebi... taehûdat ra... taehûdatê
ne wekî noka rêk û der û tebîda mekteba...
 
And a segment of our village was... [working in]
contracts... contracts not like now with roads and places
and paving schools...

70
00:06:16,000 --> 00:06:24,000
Bi kûmîra hikûmeta Osmanî... Fransiz ra, Înglîz ra... kûmir
diçû, deman ra, rêka trenê û tiştê meşî...
 
With the coal [era] of the Ottoman government... with the
French, with the English... coal was going, with time, the
train tracks and walking things...

71
00:06:24,000 --> 00:06:26,000
Wê çaxê bi kûmîra ra... tîcaretî ya ra bûn.
 
At that time with the coal [trains]... they were into trade.

72
00:06:26,000 --> 00:06:30,000
Merhele bi merhele tetawir bûn tîcarî ya gundî ya.
 
Stage by stage the village's trade developed.

73
00:06:30,000 --> 00:06:33,000
Heta noka destî me tîcaretî ya da heye.
 
Until now we have a hand in trade.

74
00:06:33,000 --> 00:06:38,000
Piştî tîcaretî yê yavaş yavaş tedrîcî yen di vî gundî da
seqafê... şehadet elmî ye...
 
After trade, slowly and gradually in this village culture...
scientific degrees...

75
00:06:38,000 --> 00:06:43,000
Bê dektûr, min... salê çil û pênca da... şehadet ketin vî
gundî, şehadê senevî...
 
Like doctors, I mean... in the year 45... degrees entered
this village, secondary school degrees...

76
00:06:43,000 --> 00:06:48,000
Wa hakeza heta noka... gundekî şehadê xwe pir in... û seqafî
xwe pir e.
 
And so on until now... it's a village with many degrees...
and its culture is abundant.

77
00:06:48,000 --> 00:06:52,000
Kadrî elmî tê heye... û wekî din jî... her tişt di gund da
heye.
 
There is scientific cadre in it... and other things too...
everything is in the village.

78
00:06:52,000 --> 00:06:55,000
Muhamî û tixtir di vî gundî da hene? Xerecîn e?
 
Are there lawyers and doctors in this village? Graduates?

79
00:06:55,000 --> 00:06:58,000
Vî gundî da... ma got ehlîn camî'în pir in...
 
In this village... I said university graduates are many...

80
00:06:58,000 --> 00:07:05,000
Mecmûek pir tixtir jî hene... Jîlê berê me û jîlê me û jîlê
pey me ra... wekî jîlê şebaba, wekî we...
 
There is a large group of doctors too... The generation
before us and our generation and the generation after us...
like the youth generation, like you...

81
00:07:05,000 --> 00:07:08,000
Em pir, ku nas nakin qiçkê kû bûn tixtir ortaq.
 
We are many, that we don't recognize whose kids became
doctors, friend.

82
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:11,000
Em dibêjin qiçkê filanî bû tixtir, em kêf dikin.
 
We say so-and-so's kid became a doctor, we rejoice.

83
00:07:11,000 --> 00:07:18,000
Em dixwazin van erşîvî çêkin. Qiçkê filanî bû muhamî, qiçkê
filanî bû istaz, bû muhendis, bû filan.
 
We want to create this archive. So-and-so's kid became a
lawyer, so-and-so's kid became a teacher, became an
engineer, became such.

84
00:07:18,000 --> 00:07:20,000
Û muhendisê me jî pir in.
 
And our engineers are also many.

85
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:27,000
Û seydelî me jî hene... Istazê me camî'în... şehadet camî'î
ye... a... bi fûrû'a kafeten cem me pir in.
 
And we have pharmacists too... Our university teachers...
university degrees... uh... in all branches are many with
us.

86
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:32,000
Tim malbeş camî'î tenê hene... tim mal... te'hîla elmî tê
hene.
 
Some households only have university graduates... some
houses... have scientific qualifications.

87
00:07:32,000 --> 00:07:37,000
Fennê vî gundî çî ye? Fennê xwe, tembîrciyê xwe?
 
What is the art of this village? Its art, its tembûr
players?

88
00:07:37,000 --> 00:07:42,000
Va gunda tembîrvanê xwe... cem me... dengbêjê me tine bûn.
 
This village, its tembûr players... with us... we didn't
have dengbêjs (bards).

89
00:07:42,000 --> 00:07:49,000
Cem me kî hebî... îbda' kir... berê vê fetrekî... ewelet
menînat da... istaz Semîr Elî bû.
 
With us who was there... who created... before this
period... in the early eighties... it was teacher Semîr Elî.

90
00:07:49,000 --> 00:07:53,000
Xwe tef fenn kir... fennan bûn, fennan Semîr Elî.
 
He devoted himself to art... he was an artist, artist Semîr
Elî.

91
00:07:53,000 --> 00:07:58,000
Paşê li merivekî me din... bi leqeb dibên Farûq... ew ji ber
wa ye.
 
Then another relative of ours... by nickname they call
Farûq... he is because of them.

92
00:07:58,000 --> 00:08:01,000
Wa şebabê din e noka... me hene.
 
And the other youth now... we have them.

93
00:08:01,000 --> 00:08:08,000
Wekî noka qîça bikimê la a... heval Hebû... wek Lawîn
Cefer... mane?
 
Like now the kids... friend Hebû... like Lawîn Cefer... you
know?

94
00:08:08,000 --> 00:08:15,000
Î katin sehê... em daxwazin genca... wekî bavê... li ser me
da... xweş tê... dewrê xwe bigrin cî xwe tijî bikin ji mer
ra.
 
They came onto the scene... we want the youth... like the
father... upon us... it feels good... to take their turn and
fill their place for us.

95
00:08:15,000 --> 00:08:16,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

96
00:08:16,000 --> 00:08:21,000
Înşallah rojê pêş da... egil cihê bilind bin, em daxwazin li
her gundekî me...
 
God willing in the days ahead... [may they] be in high
places, we wish in every village of ours...

97
00:08:21,000 --> 00:08:30,000
Xwendewanê me jî hebin, tembîrciyê me jî hebin, hunermendê
me jî hebin... Em daxwazin bi giştî em li pêş kevin...
 
We have our educated ones, our tembûr players, our
artists... We wish generally to progress...

98
00:08:30,000 --> 00:08:42,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

99
00:08:42,000 --> 00:08:52,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

100
00:08:52,000 --> 00:08:57,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

101
00:08:57,000 --> 00:09:07,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

102
00:09:07,000 --> 00:09:12,000
Hatim li Efrîn.
 
I came to Afrin.

103
00:09:12,000 --> 00:09:17,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

104
00:09:17,000 --> 00:09:30,000
Hatim li Efrîn.
 
I came to Afrin.

105
00:09:30,000 --> 00:09:33,000
Yarê yarê...
 
Oh love, oh love...

106
00:09:33,000 --> 00:09:38,000
Hatim li Efrîn.
 
I came to Afrin.

107
00:09:38,000 --> 00:09:58,000
Hatim li Efrîn.
 
I came to Afrin.

108
00:10:00,000 --> 00:10:02,000
Hûn serbiderxistina bûkê jî dikirin?
 
Did you also perform the "bringing out of the bride"
ceremony?

109
00:10:02,000 --> 00:10:03,000
Belê, serbiderxistina bûkê dikirin.
 
Yes, they used to perform the bringing out of the bride.

110
00:10:03,000 --> 00:10:07,000
Ka ji me re xeberde, serbiderxistin wextê tê çi dikirin?
Daweta tel kîl serbider dikirin?
 
Tell us about it, what did you do during the bringing out of
the bride? Did you bring her out on a wire [zip-line]
wedding style?

111
00:10:07,000 --> 00:10:10,000
Erebey tune bûn babam. Li ser pişta hêştirê, di nava kejan
de.
 
There were no cars, dear. On the back of a camel, inside a
saddle-pavilion.

112
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:12,000
Çend rojan dikirin?
 
How many days did they do it for?

113
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,000
Heft rojan dikirin.
 
They did it for seven days.

114
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:20,000
Zemanê me kêm bûn, bes zemanê berî me, wekî vê hewîlê,
hefteyekê şev û roj berxwedida.
 
In our time it was less, but in the time before us, like
this generation [referring to older times], it lasted a
week, day and night.

115
00:10:20,000 --> 00:10:24,000
Dawet hefteyekê berxwedida, lê li gund.
 
The wedding lasted a week, but in the village.

116
00:10:24,000 --> 00:10:30,000
Bes em biçûk bûn, zemanê me, ew wext teqe şof kir, [Teqeşuf:
Arabic for austerity]. Hêdî hêdî zeîf kir, kir sê rojan.
 
But we were small, in our time, that era adopted austerity.
Slowly they reduced it, made it three days.

117
00:10:30,000 --> 00:10:34,000
Paşê kirin du rojan, roja îro bûye saetek du saet, qediya
çû.
 
Then they made it two days, today it has become an hour or
two, and it's over.

118
00:10:34,000 --> 00:10:38,000
Saetek ortaq, giş merhele saî ye. Wekî ceza saî ye [Saa'i:
Arabic for courier/hasting].
 
An hour together, the whole stage is hasty. Like a hurried
punishment.

119
00:10:38,000 --> 00:10:41,000
Lê wextê daweta me li gund sê xal [nuqte] hebûn.
 
But during our weddings in the village, there were three
points [locations].

120
00:10:41,000 --> 00:10:44,000
Li sehê guleyan, sehê camiyê.
 
At the shooting field, the mosque square.

121
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:48,000
Her yekî bi hespê xwe va nîzîkî daweta xwe, li vê sehê
dikir.
 
Everyone with their horses near their wedding, would perform
in this square.

122
00:10:48,000 --> 00:10:51,000
Sê xal teqrîben me hebûn. Dawet bi rêûresm bû.
 
We had approximately three points. The wedding had rituals.

123
00:10:51,000 --> 00:10:56,000
Ê varya, roj paşîn jî bûk dianîn, yekî henekçî li vî gundî,
li wî gundî...
 
Oh yes, on the last day they brought the bride, a joker
[entertainer] from this village, or that village...

124
00:10:56,000 --> 00:11:02,000
Di anîn mala mezin, mezinê xaniyê ser du qat, di nava mezinê
xaniyê du qat re, di nava mezinê... bûk li wir hane dikir.
 
They brought her to the big house, the big two-story house,
through the big two-story house... the bride would circle
there.

125
00:11:02,000 --> 00:11:04,000
Wê tinê daweta me bi serê dibû.
 
Only then would our wedding be concluded.

126
00:11:04,000 --> 00:11:07,000
Sibê heya êvarê daweta xwe dikirin.
 
From morning until evening, they held their wedding.

127
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,000
Û li dawetê şîv da jî, tiştê alîkarî jî didan.
 
And at the wedding dinner, they also gave assistance/gifts.

128
00:11:10,000 --> 00:11:14,000
Û her kesî gûz, mîj, mêw jê ra, diçûna mala wî.
 
And everyone took walnuts, lentils, fruits for him, going to
his house.

129
00:11:14,000 --> 00:11:15,000
We henekçî jî hebûn?
 
Did you have jokers/entertainers too?

130
00:11:15,000 --> 00:11:21,000
Henekçî... em diçûn berîka... ê helbestvan, varya zêde û
zewciyê me, laqirfê dikirin, de yalla destmala me bidin.
 
Jokers... we went to the pocket... poets, or rather the
excess and pairs of us, they made jokes, "come on give us
our handkerchief."

131
00:11:21,000 --> 00:11:23,000
Destmal jî didan me.
 
They gave us handkerchiefs too.

132
00:11:23,000 --> 00:11:24,000
Erê welle.
 
Yes, indeed.

133
00:11:24,000 --> 00:11:27,000
Bi Xwedê xweş bû, her kesî tenê xwarina xwe çêdikir.
 
By God it was good, everyone made their own food.

134
00:11:27,000 --> 00:11:28,000
Adet û teqalîd...
 
Customs and traditions...

135
00:11:28,000 --> 00:11:32,000
Bêrê mesela hûru dawet li vê derê dibû, hûru dawet li vê
gêçê dibû.
 
Before, for example, a wedding would be here, a wedding
would be in this alley.

136
00:11:32,000 --> 00:11:34,000
Li sahê camiyê dibû.
 
It would be in the mosque square.

137
00:11:34,000 --> 00:11:37,000
Ere her derê ku li vê gêçê bû, li wî gêçê bû.
 
Yes, wherever it was, in this alley or that alley.

138
00:11:37,000 --> 00:11:40,000
Merhele çû. Mecmûek li gund hebû...
 
That stage passed. There was a group in the village...

139
00:11:40,000 --> 00:11:45,000
Em bêjin alemê suba, wekî mesela zabit el fellahîn, dizî
zeat, cêşê sûrî de hebû.
 
Let's say people like officers, like for example the
"peasant officers" [reference to Baathist era terminology],
agriculture, existing in the Syrian army.

140
00:11:45,000 --> 00:11:50,000
Mecmûek li gund hebû, dewrê kewreslaqê, yan dewrê fukahî
dibrin.
 
There was a group in the village, they played the role of
the "cypress branch" [rough game] or the role of comedy.

141
00:11:50,000 --> 00:11:52,000
Kerê ketûrê, yan qeşmerçî dibûn.
 
They had mules, or became clowns.

142
00:11:52,000 --> 00:11:54,000
Em giş bizzûra qeşmerliqê.
 
We are all the seeds of clowning/joking.

143
00:11:54,000 --> 00:11:58,000
Qeşmer yanî em dibêjin kerê koz, na erebî dibêjin kerê koz
[Karakoz].
 
Qeşmer means we call it "Kerê Koz", no in Arabic they call
it "Karakoz" [Puppet theater/Clown].

144
00:11:58,000 --> 00:12:01,000
Karakoz, Karakoz mam, qeşmerçî dibûn.
 
Karakoz, Karakoz uncle, they became clowns.

145
00:12:01,000 --> 00:12:06,000
We paşê, hêwaş hêwaş çû, zeîf bû, dawet teng bûn, mecal
nefes nema, were yabo.
 
And then, slowly it went away, became weak, weddings became
tight, no room to breathe remained, oh man.

146
00:12:06,000 --> 00:12:11,000
Ê dawet jî nîzîk bûn mesela, bê mala xwarina xwe çêdikir, bê
mala xwarina xwe çêdikir?
 
And weddings were close, for example, this house made their
food, that house made their food?

147
00:12:11,000 --> 00:12:12,000
Xwarin...
 
Food...

148
00:12:12,000 --> 00:12:13,000
Kî xwarin çêdikirin ji bo cîranan?
 
Who made food for the neighbors?

149
00:12:13,000 --> 00:12:14,000
Mêla xwedê dawetê.
 
The family of the wedding owner.

150
00:12:14,000 --> 00:12:19,000
Xwedê dawetê, cema mesela dibrin cem xwe, xwarina bi serê
dikirin.
 
The wedding owner, the group for example, they took them to
their place, they prepared the food.

151
00:12:19,000 --> 00:12:21,000
Ê varya, êkî li wir xew dikirin.
 
Oh yes, some slept there.

152
00:12:21,000 --> 00:12:25,000
Bûkê henekirana, sibê da rabûna daweta xwe bikirana.
 
They would joke with the bride, in the morning they would
get up and do their wedding.

153
00:12:25,000 --> 00:12:28,000
Daweta xwe jî, ê alîkariya xwe jî kom kirana.
 
Their wedding too, they would collect their assistance/gifts
too.

154
00:12:28,000 --> 00:12:34,000
Û de yalla, bimbarekî kirin û saeta we xweş, her kesî
vegeriya mala xwe ciya xwe.
 
And come on, congratulated them and have a good time,
everyone returned to their home and place.

155
00:12:34,000 --> 00:12:36,000
Adet û teqalîdê me gûhêrîn babam.
 
Our customs and traditions changed, dear.

156
00:12:36,000 --> 00:12:38,000
Lese mehela mirîk biba, dîsa nefsî şî.
 
Even if there was a dead person in the neighborhood, it was
the same thing.

157
00:12:38,000 --> 00:12:39,000
Berê xwarin dikirin?
 
Did they provide food in the past?

158
00:12:39,000 --> 00:12:40,000
Erê xwarin...
 
Yes food...

159
00:12:40,000 --> 00:12:42,000
Na na mirî na, gelê malê mirinê.
 
No no, the dead, not the dead person's family.

160
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:44,000
Gelê wê deynin, xelkê wê deynin.
 
Their people would provide it, the locals would provide it.

161
00:12:44,000 --> 00:12:50,000
Gelê malê, erê welle. Yanî jibirna dûr be, li samehela, berê
wekî dawetê pir xweş bû.
 
The family's people, yes indeed. Meaning far be it from you,
in the neighborhood, before it was very good like a wedding.

162
00:12:50,000 --> 00:12:56,000
Her kes xwarina xwe çêdikir, her kes miletê ewê mesela tê
nas dike, kî dinas dike.
 
Everyone made their own food, everyone, the people who for
example know you, whoever knows you.

163
00:12:56,000 --> 00:13:00,000
Her kesî dibir cem xwe, sifra xwe didan nan dixwarin.
 
Everyone took them to their place, set their table, ate
bread.

164
00:13:00,000 --> 00:13:03,000
Û bî tûnî. Ê noka tiştê waha nemaye.
 
And that was it. But now such things do not remain.

165
00:13:03,000 --> 00:13:06,000
Ne ê daweta ma, ne ê miriya li samehela ma.
 
Not regarding our weddings, nor regarding the dead in our
neighborhood.

166
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:10,000
Ma giden salê, soret ke eşta, xalas bî çî.
 
It's gone like the years, became a narrative like winter,
finished and gone.

167
00:13:10,000 --> 00:13:13,000
Gîjî mesref gî ser mali miriye.
 
Is all the expense now on the deceased's family?

168
00:13:13,000 --> 00:13:16,000
Lê, we çaxê, li mali mirî sivik dibû.
 
But, at that time, it was light on the deceased's family.

169
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:22,000
Em bêjin hûru me kirî, cîranê me kirî, îde kirî, îden kirî,
ê ber kirî.
 
Let's say we did it, our neighbor did it, this one did it,
that one did it, the other one did it.

170
00:13:22,000 --> 00:13:26,000
Pêncî malî, sed malî haziriya xwe dikir. Jibo mirî.
 
Fifty households, a hundred households prepared themselves.
For the deceased.

171
00:13:26,000 --> 00:13:36,000
Ne mesela, ewa ten badîna mesela, ehmabeke wekî te resmê te
heke be, bîbînim, bê gundekî pênsed malî, çarse malî hat
gundê Hec Xelîl, lazim e nan bixwe.
 
Not for example... those coming from Baadina for example, a
loved one like you, if he has status, if I see him... If a
village of 500 households, 400 households came to Hach
Khalil village, they must eat.

172
00:13:36,000 --> 00:13:41,000
Nan ne li ser milê, xwedê mirî ye. Li ser milê cîrana ye, li
ser milê gunda ye.
 
The food was not on the shoulder of the deceased's owner. It
was on the neighbors' shoulders, on the village's shoulders.

173
00:13:41,000 --> 00:13:42,000
Ewa bar sivik dikir.
 
That lightened the load.

174
00:13:42,000 --> 00:13:46,000
Noka bar giran bûye. Her tişt bûye made.
 
Now the load has become heavy. Everything has become
material.

175
00:13:46,000 --> 00:13:48,000
Zeman guherî. Ew tişt nema.
 
Time changed. Those things remained no more.

176
00:13:48,000 --> 00:13:52,000
Heta noka, ya nî miriyek bimre, divê heft rojan xwarinê bide
milet.
 
Until now, meaning if a dead person dies, he [the family]
must give food to the people for seven days.

177
00:13:52,000 --> 00:13:54,000
Heft rojan milet nanê wî dixwe.
 
For seven days the people eat his food.

178
00:13:54,000 --> 00:13:57,000
Ne bes gundê wî, der û cîran jî tên dixwin.
 
Not just his village, surroundings and neighbors also come
and eat.

179
00:13:57,000 --> 00:13:59,000
Ew barekî giran e.
 
That is a heavy load.

180
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:01,000
Em hêvîdarin ew adet rabe.
 
We hope that custom is removed.

181
00:14:01,000 --> 00:14:03,000
Mirî mir, xwedê rehma xwe lê bike.
 
The dead died, may God have mercy on him.

182
00:14:03,000 --> 00:14:06,000
Wext diyar bikin, ji saet çaran heya pêncan.
 
Specify a time, from four o'clock until five o'clock.

183
00:14:06,000 --> 00:14:08,000
Tê fatîha bixwîne û here mala xwe.
 
Come recite the Fatiha and go to your home.

184
00:14:08,000 --> 00:14:09,000
Bar giran nekin.
 
Don't make the load heavy.

185
00:14:09,000 --> 00:14:10,000
Ew barê giran e.
 
That is a heavy load.

186
00:14:10,000 --> 00:14:13,000
Îcûz yê mirî, heft heşt keçek hene, sê çar heb hene.
 
Maybe the deceased has seven or eight daughters, has three
or four.

187
00:14:13,000 --> 00:14:14,000
Tiştek li ber destê wî tune.
 
He has nothing at hand.

188
00:14:14,000 --> 00:14:17,000
Ma mecbûr e ew deyn bike, xelkê têr bike?
 
Is he forced to borrow money to feed the people?

189
00:14:17,000 --> 00:14:18,000
Wî çaxî, xelkê têr dikir.
 
At that time [in the past], the people fed [the mourners].

190
00:14:18,000 --> 00:14:20,000
Miletê cîran, alîkarî dikir.
 
The neighbor people helped.

191
00:14:20,000 --> 00:14:24,000
Sindoqa ard dianî, teneka rûn dianî, kîsekî birinc dianî.
 
Brought a box of flour, brought a tin of oil, brought a sack
of rice.

192
00:14:24,000 --> 00:14:25,000
Alîkarî dikirin.
 
They helped.

193
00:14:25,000 --> 00:14:26,000
Noka ew nema.
 
Now that is gone.

194
00:14:26,000 --> 00:14:27,000
Heyat guhorî.
 
Life changed.

195
00:14:27,000 --> 00:14:29,000
Heyat guhorî.
 
Life changed.

196
00:14:29,000 --> 00:14:31,000
Zemanê berê xweş bû babam.
 
The old times were good, dear.

197
00:14:31,000 --> 00:14:33,000
Zemanê berê, em diçûn, me digot de yalla em herin sêr bikin.
 
In the old times, we went, we said "come on let's go watch."

198
00:14:33,000 --> 00:14:35,000
Tendurustiya we ya berê çawa bû?
 
How was your health in the past?

199
00:14:35,000 --> 00:14:36,000
Saxlemiya we, nexweşî hebûn?
 
Your wellness, were there sicknesses?

200
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:37,000
Nexweşî tunebûn.
 
There were no sicknesses.

201
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:38,000
Welleh nexweşî tunebûn.
 
By God there were no sicknesses.

202
00:14:38,000 --> 00:14:42,000
Em diçûn, me kar dikir, em diçûn pembû, em diçûn nav bexça.
 
We went, we worked, we went to the cotton [fields], we went
into the orchards.

203
00:14:42,000 --> 00:14:45,000
Em diçûn me kar dikir, em dihatin, tiştekî me tunebû.
 
We went and worked, we came back, nothing was wrong with us.

204
00:14:45,000 --> 00:14:46,000
Ne di serê me de bû, ne di lingê me de bû.
 
Not in our head, nor in our legs.

205
00:14:46,000 --> 00:14:48,000
Ê noka, nexweşî pirbûye.
 
But now, sickness has increased.

206
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:52,000
Gî şekir e, gî tansiyon e, gî nexweşî, gî qolinc e.
 
It's all sugar [diabetes], all blood pressure, all sickness,
all colic/spasms.

207
00:14:52,000 --> 00:14:56,000
Heta çoka me, lingê me qata bûne, em nikarin bimeşin.
 
Even our knees, our legs are cut off [tired], we cannot
walk.

208
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:58,000
Welleh wusa bûye.
 
By God it has become like this.

209
00:14:58,000 --> 00:14:59,000
Ê berê nexweşî kêm bû.
 
Before, sickness was rare.

210
00:14:59,000 --> 00:15:01,000
Berê nexweşî kêm bûn?
 
Before sicknesses were rare?

211
00:15:01,000 --> 00:15:02,000
Kêm bûn.
 
They were rare.

212
00:15:02,000 --> 00:15:03,000
Pir kêm bûn.
 
Very rare.

213
00:15:03,000 --> 00:15:04,000
Vê nexweşiyê ji çi dibînî?
 
What do you see as the cause of this sickness?

214
00:15:04,000 --> 00:15:06,000
Ji qehir e? Ji xwarinê ye?
 
From grief/anger? From food?

215
00:15:06,000 --> 00:15:07,000
Ji qehir e.
 
From grief/anger.

216
00:15:07,000 --> 00:15:12,000
Milet, yekî diçe dûr, yekî dimre, yekî dimîne, yekî nexweş
dikeve.
 
The people, one goes far away, one dies, one remains, one
falls ill.

217
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:14,000
Yekî zaroka wî li ber çavê wî dimre.
 
One's child dies before his eyes.

218
00:15:14,000 --> 00:15:17,000
Gî qehir e, gî nexweşî ye, gî derd e.
 
It is all grief, all sickness, all pain.

219
00:15:17,000 --> 00:15:18,000
Welleh gî derd e.
 
By God it is all pain.

220
00:15:18,000 --> 00:15:21,000
Xwedê teala rehma xwe li miletê me ke.
 
May God Almighty have mercy on our people.

221
00:15:21,000 --> 00:15:23,000
Xwedê teala heqê miletê me derxîne.
 
May God Almighty bring out the rights of our people.

222
00:15:23,000 --> 00:15:27,000
Rebbê alemê, em dibêjin, xêra me û miletê me bibîne.
 
Lord of the worlds, we say, may He see the good for us and
our people.

223
00:15:27,000 --> 00:15:29,000
Çi bêjim, kurê min?
 
What can I say, my son?

224
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:31,000
Xwedê we bihêle, Xwedê emrê we dirêj ke.
 
May God keep you, may God prolong your life.

225
00:15:31,000 --> 00:15:33,000
Xwedê ciwaniyê we bişitirîne.
 
May God protect your youth.

226
00:15:33,000 --> 00:15:34,000
Gelekî spas.
 
Thank you very much.

227
00:15:34,000 --> 00:15:36,000
Xwedê we ji dê û bavê we re bihêle.
 
May God keep you for your mother and father.

228
00:15:36,000 --> 00:15:38,000
Hûn xwedî zarok in? Zarokê we hene?
 
Do you have children? Do you have kids?

229
00:15:38,000 --> 00:15:39,000
Hene.
 
We have.

230
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:43,000
Zarokê me hene, li xerîbiyê ne, hinek li vir in.
 
We have children, they are in exile [abroad], some are here.

231
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,000
Keçikê min hene, kurê min hene.
 
I have daughters, I have sons.

232
00:15:45,000 --> 00:15:51,000
Yek li Almanya ye, didu li vir in. Keçika min li Tirkiyê ye,
li Stenbolê ye.
 
One is in Germany, two are here. My daughter is in Turkey,
in Istanbul.

233
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,000
Yek li Qamişlo ye.
 
One is in Qamishli.

234
00:15:52,000 --> 00:15:54,000
Yek li vir e, ba me ye.
 
One is here, with us.

235
00:15:54,000 --> 00:15:57,000
Em dibêjin Xwedê rehma xwe li wan ke, Xwedê wan bişitirîne.
 
We say may God have mercy on them, may God protect them.

236
00:15:57,000 --> 00:15:58,000
Em çi bêjin?
 
What can we say?

237
00:15:58,000 --> 00:16:03,000
Em dibêjin Xwedê wan ji nexweşiyê bişitirîne, ji qezabela
bişitirîne.
 
We say may God protect them from sickness, protect them from
accidents and calamities.

238
00:16:03,000 --> 00:16:05,000
Em tenê duaya dikin.
 
We only pray.

239
00:16:05,000 --> 00:16:07,000
Em nikarin tiştekî bikin.
 
We cannot do anything.

240
00:16:07,000 --> 00:16:10,000
Ne destê me tê, ne em dikarin herin, ne em dikarin werin.
 
Neither does it come to our hand [we have power], nor can we
go, nor can we come.

241
00:16:10,000 --> 00:16:12,000
Em tenê duayê xêrê ji wan re dikin.
 
We only pray for good for them.

242
00:16:12,000 --> 00:16:15,000
Xwedê dilê herkesî bişewitîne, dilê me jî di nav da.
 
May God burn everyone's heart [with compassion/love], our
hearts included.

243
00:16:15,000 --> 00:16:18,000
Xwedê deriyekî xêrê li miletê me veke.
 
May God open a door of goodness for our people.

244
00:16:18,000 --> 00:16:19,000
Dê were.
 
It will come.

245
00:16:19,000 --> 00:16:21,000
Xwedê heqê me derxîne.
 
May God bring out our rights.

246
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:24,000
Tu dixwazî silava li keça xwe bikî? Vaye kamera li hemberî
te ye.
 
Do you want to send greetings to your daughter? Here is the
camera opposite you.

247
00:16:24,000 --> 00:16:26,000
Ê ez çi bikim? Ez nikarim.
 
Oh, what should I do? I cannot.

248
00:16:26,000 --> 00:16:28,000
Bêje ez silav dikim, navê wê çi ye?
 
Say "I greet...", what is her name?

249
00:16:28,000 --> 00:16:29,000
Felek e.
 
It is Felek.

250
00:16:29,000 --> 00:16:31,000
Bêje Felek, ez silavê li te dikim.
 
Say "Felek, I greet you."

251
00:16:31,000 --> 00:16:35,000
Felek, qurbana te bim, ez silavê li te dikim.
 
Felek, may I be a sacrifice for you, I greet you.

252
00:16:35,000 --> 00:16:37,000
Çavê te maç dikim.
 
I kiss your eyes.

253
00:16:37,000 --> 00:16:40,000
Xwedê te bihêle, Xwedê zarokê te bihêle.
 
May God keep you, may God keep your children.

254
00:16:40,000 --> 00:16:42,000
Xwedê te bişitirîne.
 
May God protect you.

255
00:16:42,000 --> 00:16:43,000
Ez çi bêjim qurban?
 
What should I say, my dear?

256
00:16:43,000 --> 00:16:45,000
Xwedê rehma xwe li we ke.
 
May God have mercy on you.

257
00:16:45,000 --> 00:16:47,000
Xwedê we bi hev re bihêle.
 
May God keep you together.

258
00:16:47,000 --> 00:16:49,000
Tu û mêrê xwe û zarokê xwe.
 
You and your husband and your children.

259
00:16:49,000 --> 00:16:51,000
Xwedê deriyekî xêrê li we veke.
 
May God open a door of goodness for you.

260
00:16:51,000 --> 00:16:53,000
Xwedê heqê we derxîne.
 
May God bring out your rights.

261
00:16:53,000 --> 00:16:56,000
Xwedê we bîne, em we bibînin bi çavê serê xwe.
 
May God bring you, so we see you with our own eyes.

262
00:16:56,000 --> 00:16:58,000
Em pê şa bibin.
 
So we may rejoice with it.

263
00:16:58,000 --> 00:17:00,000
Em pê kêfweş bibin.
 
So we may be happy with it.

264
00:17:00,000 --> 00:17:02,000
Tu dixwazî silava li kesekî bikî?
 
Do you want to send greetings to anyone?

265
00:17:02,000 --> 00:17:05,000
Em silavê li hemû kesên derbiderbûyî dikin.
 
We send greetings to all those who have been
displaced/exiled.

266
00:17:05,000 --> 00:17:06,000
Hemû derbiderin.
 
They are all displaced.

267
00:17:06,000 --> 00:17:08,000
Em ji wan re dibêjin "Tuyoor al Muhajira" [Erebî: Çivîkên
koçber].
 
We call them "The Migratory Birds" [Arabic].

268
00:17:08,000 --> 00:17:09,000
Çivîkên koçber in.
 
They are migratory birds.

269
00:17:09,000 --> 00:17:11,000
Ji ber zilmê, ji ber zorê revîne.
 
Fled because of oppression, because of force.

270
00:17:11,000 --> 00:17:13,000
Ne ji kêfa xwe çûne.
 
They did not go for their own pleasure.

271
00:17:13,000 --> 00:17:16,000
Kesê ji kêfa xwe diçe, diçe seyranê, diçe nêçîrê.
 
A person who goes for their own pleasure goes for a picnic,
goes hunting.

272
00:17:16,000 --> 00:17:19,000
Diçe Ewropa, diçe welatê xelkê, çi kêfa wî jê re tê?
 
Goes to Europe, goes to people's countries, what pleasure
comes to him from it?

273
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:20,000
Welatê me xweş e.
 
Our country is good.

274
00:17:20,000 --> 00:17:25,000
Bes heke welatê me, serbestî lê heba, demokrasî lê heba,
azadî lê heba.
 
Only if our country had freedom in it, had democracy in it,
had liberty in it.

275
00:17:25,000 --> 00:17:26,000
Me ew terik nedikirin.
 
We would not have abandoned it.

276
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,000
Me ew bernedida.
 
We would not have let it go.

277
00:17:28,000 --> 00:17:31,000
Çar keçê min li wir in, du kurê min li wir in.
 
Four of my daughters are there, two of my sons are there.

278
00:17:31,000 --> 00:17:34,000
Em jî li vir mane, ez û jina xwe, pîrejin û kalemêr.
 
And we remained here, me and my wife, an old woman and an
old man.

279
00:17:34,000 --> 00:17:35,000
Em tenê mane.
 
We remained alone.

280
00:17:35,000 --> 00:17:36,000
Dilê me şewitiye.
 
Our hearts are burnt.

281
00:17:36,000 --> 00:17:38,000
Lê em çi bikin? Çare nîne.
 
But what can we do? There is no solution.

282
00:17:38,000 --> 00:17:40,000
Em silavê li wan dikin. Li hemûyan dikin.
 
We greet them. We greet them all.

283
00:17:40,000 --> 00:17:43,000
Em hêvîdarin, înşallah rojekê vegerin welatê xwe.
 
We hope, God willing, one day they return to their country.

284
00:17:43,000 --> 00:17:45,000
"Al ilmu yarfa'u buyutan la 'imada laha" [Erebî: Zanist
malên bê stûn bilind dike].
 
"Knowledge raises houses that have no pillars."

285
00:17:45,000 --> 00:17:47,000
"Wal jehlu yehdimu buyutal izzi wal karami" [Erebî: Û nezanî
malên rûmet û comerdiyê xira dike].
 
"And ignorance demolishes houses of glory and generosity."

286
00:17:47,000 --> 00:17:49,000
Hûn pêşmergên me ne.
 
You are our Peshmerga [forward-to-death/freedom fighters].

287
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:50,000
Hûn çira me ne.
 
You are our light/lamp.

288
00:17:50,000 --> 00:17:52,000
Çira tenê ne bi neftê ye.
 
The lamp is not only with oil/kerosene.

289
00:17:52,000 --> 00:17:55,000
Em nikarin pêşiya xwe bibînin bê roniya we. Dîwarî dikevin.
 
We cannot see in front of us without your light. We bump
into walls.

290
00:17:55,000 --> 00:17:56,000
Fa em ji we daxwazin...
 
So we request of you...

291
00:17:56,000 --> 00:18:00,000
De ew hêsirê wê jî, Xwedê we efû bike, Xwedê destê xwe li
ser we bigire.
 
And those tears of hers too, may God forgive you, may God
place His hand over you.

292
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:04,000
Em bi kêfweş bin, li musteqbelekî zahir em şûnda we bibînin.
 
May we be happy, in a bright future may we see you again.

293
00:18:04,000 --> 00:18:06,000
We lekum tewfîq min Allah. [Erebî: Û serkeftin ji Xwedê ji
we re].
 
And success from God be yours.

294
00:18:06,000 --> 00:18:07,000
Hawa daxwaza me ye.
 
This is our wish.

295
00:18:07,000 --> 00:18:08,000
Gelek spas.
 
Thanks a lot.

296
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:09,000
Tu bi xêr hatî.
 
You are welcome.

297
00:18:09,000 --> 00:18:10,000
Xwedê we bihêle.
 
May God keep you.

298
00:18:10,000 --> 00:18:12,000
Ehlen we sehlen. Bi xêr hatî.
 
Welcome. You are welcome.

299
00:18:12,000 --> 00:18:14,000
Ser serê me, ehlen we sehlen.
 
On our heads [with respect], welcome.

300
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
Bi xatirê we, bi silametî.
 
Goodbye, go with safety.

301
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:16,000
Saeta we xweş.
 
Have a good time.

302
00:18:16,000 --> 00:18:22,000
Saeta we xweş. Ez pir kêfxweş bûm, hevalên derbasbûyî, gundî
Hec Xelîl bûn. Berê min da mala...
 
Have a good time. I was very happy, passed friends, were
from Hach Khalil village. I headed to the house of...

303
00:18:22,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Oh exile...
 
Lê xerîbiyê...

304
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:30,000
Te mala min xira kir.
 
You ruined my home.

305
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:34,000
Lê xerîbiyê...
 
Oh exile...

306
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:38,000
Te çi anî serê min.
 
What have you brought upon my head.

307
00:18:38,000 --> 00:18:44,000
Lê dayê...
 
Oh mother...

308
00:18:44,000 --> 00:18:48,000
Lê dayê...
 
Oh mother...

309
00:18:48,000 --> 00:18:52,000
Lê dayê...
 
Oh mother...

310
00:18:52,000 --> 00:18:56,000
Tu nizanî halê min.
 
You don't know my condition.

311
00:18:56,000 --> 00:19:00,000
Tu nizanî halê min.
 
You don't know my condition.

312
00:19:00,000 --> 00:19:04,000
Li vê xerîbiyê...
 
In this exile...

313
00:19:04,000 --> 00:19:07,000
Li vê xerîbiyê...
 
In this exile...

314
00:19:07,000 --> 00:19:12,000
Yê sêwî me li ber dîwaran.
 
I am an orphan against the walls.

315
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,000
Yê sêwî me li ber dîwaran.
 
I am an orphan against the walls.

316
00:19:14,000 --> 00:19:17,000
Hevalên hêja, delal, piştî em derbasî gundê Hec Xelîl bûn.
 
Dear, lovely friends, after we entered the village of Hach
Khalil.

317
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,000
Niha em li saha gundê Hec Xelîl in.
 
Now we are in the square of Hach Khalil village.

318
00:19:18,000 --> 00:19:21,000
Cama di vî gundî de yek e. Mekteb di vî gundî de didu ne.
 
There is one mosque in this village. There are two schools
in this village.

319
00:19:21,000 --> 00:19:23,000
Ibtîdayî û Îdadî.
 
Primary and Middle School.

320
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:24,000
Seydale di vî gundî de yek e.
 
There is one pharmacy in this village.

321
00:19:24,000 --> 00:19:26,000
Bazar di vî gundî de çênabe.
 
No bazaar [market] takes place in this village.

322
00:19:26,000 --> 00:19:29,000
Seydaliya vî gundî jî, meireq [mereq] bi xwe re heye.
 
The pharmacy of this village also has curiosity/interest
with it.

323
00:19:29,000 --> 00:19:30,000
Niha em ê derbasî cem bibin.
 
Now we will enter it.

324
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:33,000
Ji derveyî gundê Hec Xelîl, derbasî cem vê seydalî dibin.
 
From outside Hach Khalil village, they enter this pharmacy.

325
00:19:33,000 --> 00:19:35,000
Ka em ê ha...
 
Let us see...

326
00:19:35,000 --> 00:19:36,000
Selam Aleykum.
 
Peace be upon you.

327
00:19:36,000 --> 00:19:37,000
We Aleykum Selam.
 
And upon you peace.

328
00:19:37,000 --> 00:19:38,000
Allah ya'tîk el afiye.
 
May God give you health.

329
00:19:38,000 --> 00:19:39,000
Allah yeafîk ya rab.
 
May God heal you, oh Lord.

330
00:19:39,000 --> 00:19:40,000
Kîfkom? Kîf sehetkom?
 
How are you? How is your health?

331
00:19:40,000 --> 00:19:41,000
Wallah elhemdullah.
 
By God, praise be to God.

332
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:43,000
Allah yisellmek ya rab. Allah ybarik fîkom cemîan ya rab.
 
May God save you, oh Lord. May God bless you all, oh Lord.

333
00:19:43,000 --> 00:19:44,000
Allah yisellmek ya rab.
 
May God save you, oh Lord.

334
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:47,000
Ana Xelîl min qeryet Baadina. Endî qanat YouTube.
 
I am Khalil from Baadina village. I have a YouTube channel.

335
00:19:47,000 --> 00:19:50,000
Am na'mil muqabalat el aam, we cîna fitna ela hal deiaa.
 
We are doing general interviews, and we came and entered
this village.

336
00:19:50,000 --> 00:19:53,000
Ê ehlen we sehlen, şerrefna bi wicûdkom.
 
Oh welcome, we are honored by your presence.

337
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:56,000
We fîkom ehlen we sehlen, we bi ehl hal deiaa inşallah.
 
And welcome to you, and to the people of this village, God
willing.

338
00:19:56,000 --> 00:19:57,000
Allah yisellmek ya rab.
 
May God save you, oh Lord.

339
00:19:57,000 --> 00:20:00,000
Hella haliyen, bi Hec Xelîl ma fî xêr seydaliye wahde?
 
Now currently, in Hach Khalil there is no other pharmacy but
one?

340
00:20:00,000 --> 00:20:02,000
نعم موجود، هي نعم.
 
Yes, it is here, yes.

341
00:20:02,000 --> 00:20:10,000
إي جينا فتنا بدك تحكيلنا عن الوضع الدعاوي، الصيدلية يعني
الشغل الأمور كيف ماشية؟
 
We came in, you want to tell us about the pharmaceutical
situation, the pharmacy, how is the work going?

342
00:20:10,000 --> 00:20:21,000
هلا نحن بشكل عام عنا نحن هالصيدلية فتحناها من تقريباً...
صارلها تقريباً شي ست سنين هون أنا موجود بهالصيدلية هي.
 
Well, generally, we have this pharmacy, we opened it
about... it's been about six years that I've been here in
this pharmacy.

343
00:20:21,000 --> 00:20:30,000
كان في قبل بتعرف وضع طريق مسكر باتجاه حلب أو باتجاه الشام أو
باتجاه المناطق اللي بكون فيها متوسع مجال الطبي.
 
Before, you know, the road was closed towards Aleppo or
towards Damascus or towards areas where the medical field is
expanded.

344
00:20:30,000 --> 00:20:34,000
صرنا نشتغل... هي بالأول وبالأخير هو عامل إنساني.
 
We started working... first and foremost, it is a
humanitarian work.

345
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:38,000
وليس... يختلف عن أي عامل، هو عامل إنساني.
 
And not... it differs from any other worker, it is a
humanitarian worker.

346
00:20:38,000 --> 00:20:43,000
تعتمد على... يعني طبيعة البشر هون طبيعة عايشة عالفطرة.
 
It depends on... you know, the nature of the people here is
living on instinct.

347
00:20:43,000 --> 00:20:52,000
تمام... حسب نوع كل مرض يجينا قدر المستطاع كنا نتعامل مع أي
مرض كان...
 
Okay... depending on the type of every illness that comes to
us, as much as possible, we dealt with whatever illness it
was...

348
00:20:52,000 --> 00:20:56,000
ويعني والحمد لله الأمور يعني ماشية بشكل عام.
 
And, praise be to God, things are generally going well.

349
00:20:56,000 --> 00:21:04,000
هلا أنا قبل ما إجي عحج خليل أنا بعرف كتير من أهالي باعديلي
ومن غير أهالي باعديلي الخصوصي بيجو لهون لحج خليل بس مشان يجو
لعند...
 
Now, before I came to Hec Xelîl, I know many people from
Baadînli and other than Baadînli specifically come here to
Hec Xelîl just to come to...

350
00:21:04,000 --> 00:21:05,000
صيدلي.
 
A pharmacist.

351
00:21:05,000 --> 00:21:10,000
صيدلي. يعني شو السبب عطينا السر وفي كتير عالم تمدحك يعني
بالموضوع.
 
A pharmacist. So what is the reason? Give us the secret, and
many people praise you in this regard.

352
00:21:10,000 --> 00:21:20,000
هلا إنه نحن نقطة أساسية انتشر عنا كتير مثلاً... إذا شفتو
اتضح موضوع إنه كل إنسان كان يفتح صيدلية، مو كل إنسان بيفتح
صيدلية هو يعني صيدلي.
 
Well, we are a basic point, it spread a lot among us, for
example... if you saw, it became clear that everyone was
opening a pharmacy, not everyone who opens a pharmacy is
actually a pharmacist.

353
00:21:20,000 --> 00:21:27,000
ومو كل من بيعرف يقرأ نوع دوا... يعني بيعرف يعطي دوا، ولكن
الدوا في مكانه.
 
And not everyone who knows how to read a type of medicine...
knows how to give medicine, but the medicine must be in its
place.

354
00:21:27,000 --> 00:21:35,000
في مكان المرض. وليس إنه والله أنا يالله مسيك هذا دوا ومع
السلامة. لا، هون الدوا في مكانه إن شاء الله.
 
In the place of the illness. And not just, "Here, take this
medicine and goodbye." No, here the medicine is in its
place, God willing.

355
00:21:35,000 --> 00:21:39,000
وإن شاء الله ما نقصر مع إنسان عالمنطقة بشكل عام.
 
And God willing, we won't fall short with anyone in the
region in general.

356
00:21:39,000 --> 00:21:41,000
الله يجزيك الخير وبارك الله فيك.
 
May God reward you with good and God bless you.

357
00:21:41,000 --> 00:21:42,000
الله يسلمك يارب ويحفظك.
 
May God save you and protect you.

358
00:21:42,000 --> 00:21:49,000
إي حتى من شوي قبل ما فوت عالصيدلية شفت سيارة برا الصيدلية هو
زلمة جاي من باعديلي.
 
Yes, even a little while ago before I entered the pharmacy,
I saw a car outside the pharmacy, a man coming from
Baadînli.

359
00:21:49,000 --> 00:21:53,000
يعني عالم من باعديلي وقلتلك برات باعديلي حتى بحج خليل قالولي
هذا الشي.
 
I mean people from Baadînli, and I told you outside
Baadînli, even in Hec Xelîl they told me this.

360
00:21:53,000 --> 00:21:58,000
يعني عالم بروح بينزل عالمشافي وما بيستفيد لفا لما بيجي عند
الصيدلي...
 
I mean people go down to the hospitals and don't benefit, so
when they come to the pharmacist...

361
00:21:58,000 --> 00:22:01,000
عندك مثلاً عند حضرتك وبيستفيد يعني هذا الشي كويس كتير ومنيح.
 
To you, for example, to your honor, and they benefit, so
this is very good and excellent.

362
00:22:01,000 --> 00:22:07,000
إن شاء الله يكون يعني هاي... يعني خدمة أساسية هي قلتلك من
الأول الحديث هي عامل إنساني.
 
God willing, this is... a basic service, I told you from the
beginning of the conversation, it is a humanitarian work.

363
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:13,000
وقت بدك تتعامل مع إنسان إنسانياً غير ما إنك تتعامل مع إنسان
مادياً.
 
When you deal with a human humanely, it's different from
dealing with a human materially.

364
00:22:13,000 --> 00:22:16,000
أو غير نوع تاني شي بالنسبة لهالموضوع هادا.
 
Or any other type regarding this subject.

365
00:22:16,000 --> 00:22:24,000
ووقت الإنسان اللي بدو يجي من باعديلي يجي من منطقة أبعد من
منطقة أبعد إذن أنا عم بستفيد عندك.
 
And when a person comes from Baadînli, comes from a further
area, from a further area, then "I am benefiting from you."

366
00:22:24,000 --> 00:22:26,000
أنا وقت عم بستفيد عندك برجع لعندك.
 
When I benefit from you, I come back to you.

367
00:22:26,000 --> 00:22:35,000
بغض النظر... وفي عنا أطباء الحمد لله يعني في عفرين في أطباء
شاملين في كافة الاختصاصات ومنهم بروح ومنهم بيجي.
 
Regardless... and we have doctors, praise be to God, in
Afrin there are comprehensive doctors in all specialties,
some go and some come.

368
00:22:35,000 --> 00:22:40,000
هون صفا نحن منطقة يعني تقريباً جبلية منطقة مقطوعة منطقة كذا.
 
Here we became an area, practically mountainous, a cut-off
area, such an area.

369
00:22:40,000 --> 00:22:50,000
يعني وقت عم نلاقي مثلاً بغض النظر غير أنا منلاقي صيدلي ما...
يعني فهمان... فهمان مثلاً موضوعه...
 
So when we find, for example, regardless other than me, we
find a pharmacist who is... you know, understanding...
understanding his subject, for example...

370
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:59,000
إي عم نستفيد عنده أحسن ما إنه يعني مثلاً نروح لعند إنسان
يعني يبيعنا دوا بالمشرمحي يبيعنا دوا.
 
Yes, we benefit from him better than, for example, going to
a person who just sells us medicine, bluntly, sells us
medicine.

371
00:22:59,000 --> 00:23:04,000
إي الحمد لله في... في عنا هون شباب من الضيعة حج خليل يعني...
 
Yes, praise be to God, there are... there are young men here
from the village of Hec Xelîl, I mean...

372
00:23:04,000 --> 00:23:15,000
كمان هني ساعدوني لحتى وصل لهالنقطة هاي... يعني قاموا بإنشاء
المبنى الدكان وحتى أمنولي سكن هون...
 
They also helped me to reach this point... they constructed
the building, the shop, and even secured accommodation for
me here...

373
00:23:15,000 --> 00:23:17,000
إي في منهم كتير كتر الله خيرهم.
 
Yes, there are many of them, may God increase their good.

374
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:26,000
وفي عنا أخوة يعني الحمد لله هون يعني وصلونا لنحسن نفتح مثلاً
موضوع الصيدلية لأن إمكانية المحل ما كانت في.
 
And we have brothers, praise be to God, here who helped us
to be able to open, for example, the pharmacy, because the
capability for the shop wasn't there.

375
00:23:26,000 --> 00:23:28,000
تمام، والسكن ما كان في.
 
Okay, and accommodation wasn't there.

376
00:23:28,000 --> 00:23:32,000
إي الحمد لله في شباب هون يعني لسه فيهم خير وبركة الحمد لله.
 
Yes, praise be to God, there are young men here who still
have good and blessing, praise be to God.

377
00:23:32,000 --> 00:23:34,000
الله يجزيك الخير ويبارك فيهم يارب.
 
May God reward you with good and bless them.

378
00:23:34,000 --> 00:23:36,000
الله يسلمك ويبارك في عمرك.
 
May God save you and bless your life.

379
00:23:36,000 --> 00:23:47,000
هلا اللي بحج خليل خبروني إنه حتى لو مثلاً صار عندهم حالة
إسعاف لا سمح الله يعني حتى إن كان ساعة وحدة بالليل بيجو
بيدقوا عليك بتفيق وبتخلصهم...
 
Now, those in Hec Xelîl told me that even if, for example,
they had an emergency case, God forbid, even if it was one
o'clock at night, they come and knock on your door, you wake
up and sort them out...

380
00:23:47,000 --> 00:23:57,000
بالضبط يعني أمرار مو من حج خليل ومن غير حج خليل يعني هذا
يعني سميوا بملائكة الرحمة.
 
Exactly, sometimes not from Hec Xelîl and from other than
Hec Xelîl, I mean this, they were named Angels of Mercy.

381
00:23:57,000 --> 00:24:05,000
المجال الطبي ملائكة الرحمة. ليش؟ لأن أنا وقت عم بطلع معك
الساعة وحدة الساعة تنتين الساعة تلاتة أنا طالع مشان إسعافك.
 
The medical field is Angels of Mercy. Why? Because when I go
out with you at one o'clock, two o'clock, three o'clock, I
am going out to aid you.

382
00:24:05,000 --> 00:24:11,000
إذا حسنت مثلاً إسعفك أو وصلك لنقطة طبية مثلاً تسعفك.
 
If I could, for example, aid you or get you to a medical
point that can aid you.

383
00:24:11,000 --> 00:24:14,000
يعني هاي نقطة أساسية ما في مشكلة.
 
I mean, this is a basic point, there is no problem.

384
00:24:14,000 --> 00:24:17,000
وقت بيكون الإنسان بحاجة إسعاف مثلاً بطلع معه.
 
When a person is in need of emergency aid, for example, I go
out with him.

385
00:24:17,000 --> 00:24:25,000
بطلع معه الساعة وحدة تنتين تلاتة والعالم يعني بتعرف إنه
هالنقطة هاي يعني أهم نقطة بالنسبة لإلهم.
 
I go out with him at one, two, three o'clock, and people
know that this point is the most important point for them.

386
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:35,000
يعني لا... يعني موضوع الليل ولد سخن ولد ارتفعت حرارته يعني
قدر المستطاع منحسن نساعده عبين مثلاً ما...
 
I mean no... I mean the issue of the night, a child got a
fever, a child's temperature rose, as much as possible we
can help him until, for example...

387
00:24:35,000 --> 00:24:44,000
يقوم بإجراءات تحليلات طبية أو مثلاً استشارة طبيب أطفال أو
استشارة طبيب داخلية يعني ما شابه ذلك بهي النقطة.
 
He undergoes medical analysis procedures or, for example,
consulting a pediatrician or an internist, or things like
that in this regard.

388
00:24:44,000 --> 00:24:49,000
إي أهلاً وسهلاً وبتشرفونا وميت السلامة.
 
Yes, welcome, you honor us, and a hundred welcomes.

389
00:24:49,000 --> 00:24:52,000
بدي سلامتكم والله يحفظكم وشكراً لجهودكم.
 
I wish for your safety, may God protect you, and thank you
for your efforts.

390
00:24:52,000 --> 00:24:54,000
الله يسلمك على راسي.
 
May God save you, on my head (my pleasure).

391
00:24:54,000 --> 00:24:57,000
ما عندك مشكلة نعرض هاي الحلقة على قناة اليوتيوب؟
 
You don't have a problem with us showing this episode on the
YouTube channel?

392
00:24:57,000 --> 00:24:58,000
ما في أية مشكلة إن شاء الله.
 
There is no problem at all, God willing.

393
00:24:58,000 --> 00:25:02,000
ما عندك مشكلة نحط الرقم هون؟ إذا بيحس حدا بدو يتواصل معك.
 
You don't have a problem if we put the number here? If
someone feels they want to contact you.

394
00:25:02,000 --> 00:25:03,000
ما في مشكلة تكرم.
 
No problem, you're welcome.

395
00:25:03,000 --> 00:25:06,000
تمام وهلأ مناخد كم لقطة من الصيدلية كمان.
 
Okay, and now we will take a few shots of the pharmacy as
well.

396
00:25:06,000 --> 00:25:26,000
تكرم عينك الله يسلمك.
 
You're welcome, may God save you.

397
00:26:46,000 --> 00:26:48,000
Tu bi xêr hatî.
 
Welcome.

398
00:26:48,000 --> 00:26:49,000
Bi xêr hatin.
 
Welcome.

399
00:26:49,000 --> 00:26:50,000
Tu çewa yî?
 
How are you?

400
00:26:50,000 --> 00:26:55,000
Elhemdulilah wextekî rehetî ye elhemdulilah.
 
Praise be to God, it is a comfortable time, praise be to
God.

401
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:58,000
Ez hatim cem te min got belkî qehwekê ji destê te vexwim.
 
I came to you, I said maybe I would drink a coffee from your
hand.

402
00:26:58,000 --> 00:27:02,000
Ser çava, qehwe jî heye, çay jî heye, nan jî heye.
 
With pleasure, there is coffee, there is tea, there is
bread.

403
00:27:02,000 --> 00:27:03,000
Hûn bi xêr hatin.
 
Welcome.

404
00:27:03,000 --> 00:27:05,000
Tu kurê kê yî?
 
Whose son are you?

405
00:27:05,000 --> 00:27:07,000
Ez bi xwe ji gundê Baadîno me.
 
I am personally from the village of Baadînli.

406
00:27:07,000 --> 00:27:08,000
Ji Baadîna?
 
From Baadînli?

407
00:27:08,000 --> 00:27:10,000
Ji Baadîna.
 
From Baadînli.

408
00:27:10,000 --> 00:27:11,000
Gundê Ehmedê Seydê.
 
Village of Ahmed Seyde.

409
00:27:11,000 --> 00:27:12,000
Gundê Ehmedê Seydê.
 
Village of Ahmed Seyde.

410
00:27:12,000 --> 00:27:15,000
Tu gundê Baadîno nas dikî?
 
Do you know the village of Baadînli?

411
00:27:15,000 --> 00:27:23,000
Ehlen we sehlen... Gundê Hec Xelîl ji me razî be.
 
Welcome... May the village of Hec Xelîl be pleased with us.

412
00:27:23,000 --> 00:27:29,000
Xaltîka Fîdan tu hinekî ji me re xeber de.
 
Aunt Fidan, tell us a little.

413
00:27:29,000 --> 00:27:38,000
Wele roj elhemdulilah, noka emr çûye, roj rind bibe emr
çûye.
 
Well the days, praise be to God, now age is gone, even if
the days become good, age is gone.

414
00:27:38,000 --> 00:27:41,000
Wexta emr rind roj çetin bûn. Çetin bûn.
 
When the age was good (young), the days were hard. They were
hard.

415
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:44,000
Me çi kar heye me gih kiriye.
 
Whatever work there was, we did it all.

416
00:27:44,000 --> 00:27:53,000
Ji palo, ji zeytûna, ji kinşiştnê, ji dakuyandinê, ji pez...
 
From labor, from olives, from washing clothes, from beating
(washing), from sheep...

417
00:27:53,000 --> 00:27:56,000
Hilîn û danîna pez, her tiştekî yanî me tiştekî berdayî
tine.
 
Taking up and putting down sheep, everything, I mean we
didn't leave anything undone.

418
00:27:56,000 --> 00:27:59,000
Û mi dirûn dikir a xeyata bûm.
 
And I used to sew, I was a seamstress.

419
00:27:59,000 --> 00:28:00,000
Te çi karî dikir?
 
What work did you do?

420
00:28:00,000 --> 00:28:01,000
Mi rûxangirê didan va, rûxangê spî.
 
I used to sew bed covers, white bed covers.

421
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:02,000
Tu li ser makînê jî şixulî?
 
Did you work on the machine too?

422
00:28:02,000 --> 00:28:04,000
Li ser makînê jî şixulîm, cihê spî. Ev karê me gih kiriye.
 
I worked on the machine too, white bedding. We did all this
work.

423
00:28:04,000 --> 00:28:06,000
Ev porê te yê spî nîşana wê ye?
 
Is this white hair of yours a sign of that?

424
00:28:06,000 --> 00:28:07,000
Nîşana wê ye.
 
It is a sign of that.

425
00:28:07,000 --> 00:28:11,000
Û noka jî emr çûye û wela rewş rind bibe emr çû.
 
And now age is gone, and well, even if the situation becomes
good, age is gone.

426
00:28:11,000 --> 00:28:14,000
Heta îş rind be, lê emr diçe.
 
Even if the job is good, but age goes.

427
00:28:14,000 --> 00:28:15,000
Wele emr diçe.
 
Yes, age goes.

428
00:28:15,000 --> 00:28:16,000
Te heyata xwe li ku derbas kir? Li vir?
 
Where did you spend your life? Here?

429
00:28:16,000 --> 00:28:20,000
Heyata min cefa, wele me pir derbas kir, ne hindik.
 
My life was hardship, well we went through a lot, not a
little.

430
00:28:20,000 --> 00:28:21,000
Gundî Hec Xelîl dibêjin...
 
The villagers of Hec Xelîl say...

431
00:28:21,000 --> 00:28:27,000
Em cîranê we ne. Wek noka cemaat li gunda ortax genim
dikoletin, simaqê jê dikin.
 
We are your neighbors. Like now, the community in the
villages used to harvest wheat together, pick sumac.

432
00:28:27,000 --> 00:28:33,000
Ewa wele noka berê dikirin noka ew tiştana giha rakirin.
Rakirin.
 
Well, they used to do that before, now they removed all
those things. Removed.

433
00:28:33,000 --> 00:28:41,000
Berê genim, ba dikoletin, cêncî, ba dikirin, destarê malê me
dikuta, me ar bo dikir, me hêltînan dida, û noka tişt tune.
 
Before, wheat, they harvested, threshing, they winnowed, we
ground with the hand-mill at home, we made flour, we made
dough, and now there is nothing.

434
00:28:41,000 --> 00:28:42,000
Noka tiştekî wano tune.
 
Now there is nothing like that.

435
00:28:42,000 --> 00:28:43,000
Tiştekî wano tune.
 
There is nothing like that.

436
00:28:43,000 --> 00:28:44,000
Tu ji qîza xwe hez dikî an ji... Qurbanê spî şêrê min î hat?
 
Do you love your daughters or... My sacrifice, my white lion
came?

437
00:28:44,000 --> 00:28:46,000
Bavo qîzka me, wez qurbana spî şêrê min î hat. Mla were.
 
Oh father, our daughter, I am a sacrifice, my white lion
came. Come here.

438
00:28:46,000 --> 00:28:52,000
Ewa qîzk bînon, me diçû bîra Elwîtê, ef diçû bîra Sînê, me
diçû Lçê tîno, bi kero av tîno dihotin lo.
 
Those daughters brought... we went to the well of Elwît,
they went to the well of Sîn, we went to Lçê (spring?),
brought water by donkeys, they came, oh my.

439
00:28:52,000 --> 00:28:56,000
Û her tiştek me dî ye elhemdulilah.
 
And we have seen everything, praise be to God.

440
00:28:56,000 --> 00:28:58,000
Û kincik bo jî wegî bi desta dişûştin.
 
And clothes too, you washed them all by hand.

441
00:28:58,000 --> 00:28:59,000
Wele bi desta dişûştin erê wele.
 
Yes, we washed by hand, yes indeed.

442
00:28:59,000 --> 00:29:00,000
Û karê heyata berê we cefa derbas kir.
 
And the work of the past life, you passed it in hardship.

443
00:29:00,000 --> 00:29:02,000
Wele bêtûnî bî.
 
Yes, it was complete (hardship).

444
00:29:02,000 --> 00:29:07,000
Elhemdulilah noka jî em qelxon a xêrin, îşta... wada... can
çû.
 
Praise be to God, now we are old people of good, well...
so... the soul is gone.

445
00:29:07,000 --> 00:29:09,000
Te çend qîz û kur mezin kirin Xaltîka Fîdan?
 
How many daughters and sons did you raise, Aunt Fidan?

446
00:29:09,000 --> 00:29:18,000
Bi Xwedê yo lim, deh û pênc sala qîzka min tine bûn. Deh û
pênc sala şûnda Xwedê wa bide, pênc qîzika min hene, sê law
û du qîz.
 
By God, for fifteen years I had no children. After fifteen
years God gave them, I have five children, three boys and
two girls.

447
00:29:18,000 --> 00:29:19,000
Xwedê ji te ra bihêle.
 
May God keep them for you.

448
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,000
Gil cem te ne lê?
 
Are they all with you?

449
00:29:20,000 --> 00:29:23,000
Wele lawik her sê li vir in li Sûriyê ne. Yek li Efrîn
rûniştî...
 
Well the boys, all three are here in Syria. One lives in
Afrin...

450
00:29:23,000 --> 00:29:24,000
Û du?
 
And two?

451
00:29:24,000 --> 00:29:28,000
Û du jî li virol li çarşê rûniştî, o li virol xwar rûniştî.
 
And two live right here in the market, he lives right here
down below.

452
00:29:28,000 --> 00:29:29,000
Erê.
 
Yes.

453
00:29:29,000 --> 00:29:30,000
Bas qîzk?
 
But daughters?

454
00:29:30,000 --> 00:29:33,000
Û qîzk jî zewicîne, çûne ser nesîbê xwe, li Tirkiyê ne.
 
And daughters are married, they went to their destiny, they
are in Turkey.

455
00:29:33,000 --> 00:29:34,000
Li Tirkiyê ne.
 
They are in Turkey.

456
00:29:34,000 --> 00:29:38,000
Elmesîl kê ne, pir kêfxweş bin, li kîmê ne bira nesîbê wac
gindora bişîne.
 
Anyway, whoever they are, let them be very happy, wherever
they are, let their destiny send them rolling back (good
fortune).

457
00:29:38,000 --> 00:29:39,000
Ji qîzara?
 
For the daughters?

458
00:29:39,000 --> 00:29:40,000
Ji qîzara, ji lawara.
 
For the daughters, for the sons.

459
00:29:40,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Law li cem min in, ha ro me dibînin.
 
The sons are with me, they see us every day.

460
00:29:42,000 --> 00:29:44,000
Ma tu ji qîza ra zêdetir hez dikî an ji lawa ra?
 
Do you love the daughters more or the sons?

461
00:29:44,000 --> 00:29:45,000
Wele...
 
Well...

462
00:29:45,000 --> 00:29:54,000
Ji me ra silam kin, qîzkê min Xwedê canê sax bidin, seata we
xweş, qîzkê gundîyê belê, ewa belê.
 
Say hi to us, my daughters, may God give you a healthy soul,
have a good time, daughters of the village, yes, indeed yes.

463
00:29:54,000 --> 00:29:56,000
Elhemdulilah bereket versin, ji rû ra.
 
Praise be to God, may He give blessing, from the face
(sincerely).

464
00:29:56,000 --> 00:30:00,000
Xaltîka Fîdan tiştekî mera xeber de, noka wextê mewsîmê
mastî kêmandî ye.
 
Aunt Fidan, tell us something, now is the season of strained
yogurt.

465
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:04,000
Mamê Hecxelîlî çewa mastê xwe, kemadî çêdikin? Têkşînin mera
hewal de.
 
Auntie of Hacxelil, how do they make their yogurt, their
dairy? Tell us about it, friend.

466
00:30:04,000 --> 00:30:08,000
De mastê xwe, şîrê xwe germ dikin, bimeyînin.
 
Well, they heat their yogurt, their milk, and let it
ferment.

467
00:30:08,000 --> 00:30:13,000
Meyî, emê... rokê du roki mastî bêlin.
 
Once fermented, we... leave the yogurt for a day or two.

468
00:30:13,000 --> 00:30:21,000
Paşê em... hine hine di serqin, moxê xwe dikine, hine hine
di tevdin berdin tûr, emê di tûr da jî bi neşifînin.
 
Then we... some skim the top, taking the cream, some stir it
and pour it into a sack, and we drain/dry it in the sack.

469
00:30:21,000 --> 00:30:25,000
û paşê em dihelînin, em dikelînin.
 
And then we melt it, we boil it.

470
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:29,000
Gerek ta mastê xwe meyand xelkî fîdan, te çend roj tûrkê,
berê dikirin tûr?
 
When you fermented your yogurt, people of Fidan, how many
days in the sack, did they use sacks before?

471
00:30:29,000 --> 00:30:30,000
Ê em dikin tûr işte, ne di...
 
Yes, we put it in a sack, not in...

472
00:30:30,000 --> 00:30:32,000
Te çend roj man gerek têda be?
 
How many days must it stay in there?

473
00:30:32,000 --> 00:30:35,000
Heta ney rind dineşife, hewa ava şûşê jê darre.
 
Until it dries well, until that whey water drains from it.

474
00:30:35,000 --> 00:30:39,000
Paşê em avan xwe pak dikin û em dikelînin.
 
Then we clean our [utensils/hands] and we boil it.

475
00:30:39,000 --> 00:30:43,000
û piştî de da sêr, çî, te keland, sor bî gerek te hîlî?
 
And after putting garlic, what, you boiled it, once it's
red, you must leave it?

476
00:30:43,000 --> 00:30:46,000
Lê, em sor bî, em radikin, dikin qetremîzê xwe û radikin.
 
Yes, once it's red, we pick it up, put it in our jars and
store it away.

477
00:30:46,000 --> 00:30:47,000
Te îsal çêkir mastê kemadî ne?
 
Did you make dairy yogurt this year or not?

478
00:30:47,000 --> 00:30:49,000
Me çêkir welle.
 
We made it, by God.

479
00:30:49,000 --> 00:30:50,000
Me çêkiriye.
 
We have made it.

480
00:30:50,000 --> 00:30:52,000
û mîs paşiyê, noha mîsîmî dimsî bacana jî çêdikin, dimsî...
 
And likewise, now I hear they make tomato paste as well,
paste...

481
00:30:52,000 --> 00:30:58,000
Lê dimsî benadûrê jî işte, em îna... werin benadûrê xwe
bişûn, hûr kin, xoyê kin.
 
Yes, tomato paste too, exactly... we bring our tomatoes,
wash them, chop them, salt them.

482
00:30:58,000 --> 00:31:03,000
û paşê jî mista, eyn mista, noha xesale ye, em li xesalê
dixin û em dineşifînin.
 
And then just like yogurt, exactly like yogurt, now there
are washing machines [spinners], we put it in the spinner
and dry it.

483
00:31:03,000 --> 00:31:05,000
û yên bîbera jî, wana leçar e?
 
And the pepper ones, are those strictly for the sick/diet?

484
00:31:05,000 --> 00:31:09,000
Lê bîbera jî em çêdikin, leçar e, dû per me yên mişmişan
çêkir.
 
Yes, we make peppers too, strictly [or 'leçar' type], we
made two loads of apricots.

485
00:31:09,000 --> 00:31:10,000
Î qers?
 
The pressed/dried ones?

486
00:31:10,000 --> 00:31:14,000
Emê qor bi qordîn in di leganê da, şekirê xwe pê werkin.
 
We pit them one by one into the basin, pour sugar over them.

487
00:31:14,000 --> 00:31:21,000
Heta sibê da bêlin, bi wê avê genda, kelke di yavê xin û
rokê du roj jî ber tavê dan.
 
Leave them until morning, with that own juice/water, boil
them once in that juice, and place them in the sun for a day
or two.

488
00:31:21,000 --> 00:31:23,000
Î denî mistoyî, em mibaşer.
 
The yogurt ones, we [do] directly.

489
00:31:23,000 --> 00:31:29,000
Mist didin... û sîzokê radikin û em dikelînin, sor bî em
radikin.
 
We put the yogurt... and add garlic/herbs and we boil it,
when it's red we store it.

490
00:31:29,000 --> 00:31:31,000
Ewe.
 
That's it.

491
00:31:31,000 --> 00:31:38,000
Jîna mirazê me... wekî gotî qîçka me Xwedê... te te'lî ya,
ew giyal wa namîne, ew jî li me namîne.
 
Our life's wish... as said, our daughter, God... you know
the bitterness, that grass won't stay like that, and it
won't stay with us either.

492
00:31:38,000 --> 00:31:43,000
Heve, noşî da, emrê mi bî hefte û sê, hefte û çar sal, emrê
me yê hene.
 
That is it, in health, my age is seventy-three, seventy-four
years, that is our age.

493
00:31:43,000 --> 00:31:45,000
Te mehiya dinyê da tûneye.
 
There is no greed in the world [for me].

494
00:31:45,000 --> 00:31:50,000
Te mehiya ma, qîçka me Xwedê ji me ra bihêle, em te'lî û
gendiya nebînin, hewa.
 
Our greed [wish] is, may God keep our daughter for us, that
we don't see bitterness and corruption, that's it.

495
00:31:50,000 --> 00:31:52,000
Amin, inşalla nebînî.
 
Amen, God willing you won't see it.

496
00:31:52,000 --> 00:31:58,000
Xelkî Fîdan berê gazindê, Temir Tatê gotin, mehal, te li me
hene qusûrî efû ke, em hatin dore...
 
People of Fidan used to complain, they told Temer Tat,
impossible... forgive us if we have any shortcomings, we
came around...

497
00:31:58,000 --> 00:32:00,000
Mû seheta te xweş, Xwedê ji we razî be.
 
Well, health to you, may God be pleased with you.

498
00:32:00,000 --> 00:32:03,000
Gotinê me tûne ne, Xwedê ji we razî be, sehet xweş.
 
We have nothing else to say, may God be pleased with you,
good health.

499
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:23,000
[Instrumental Music]
 
[Instrumental Music]

500
00:33:16,000 --> 00:33:17,000
Merheba.
 
Hello.

501
00:33:17,000 --> 00:33:18,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

502
00:33:18,000 --> 00:33:19,000
Navê te bi xêr?
 
Your name, please?

503
00:33:19,000 --> 00:33:21,000
Navê me Esmet. Lorî zêna Elî.
 
My name is Asmat. Son of Zena Ali.

504
00:33:21,000 --> 00:33:22,000
Bavê?
 
Father [of]?

505
00:33:22,000 --> 00:33:23,000
Bavê Mehmûd Elî.
 
Father of Mahmoud Ali.

506
00:33:23,000 --> 00:33:26,000
Bavê Mehmûd Elî. Ehlen we sehlen, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
Father of Mahmoud Ali. Welcome, may God be pleased with you.

507
00:33:26,000 --> 00:33:27,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, ehlen we sehlen, ser serê me, ser çavê
me.
 
May God be pleased with you, welcome, upon our head, upon
our eyes [you are welcome].

508
00:33:27,000 --> 00:33:29,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

509
00:33:29,000 --> 00:33:33,000
Ez Hecxelîlş, gundî Hecxelîl, kanê hotim... rewş we çawa ye,
nîvandorê gundî Hecxelîlî?
 
I am from Hacxelil too, villager of Hacxelil, where I
came... how is your situation, the surroundings of Hacxelil
village?

510
00:33:33,000 --> 00:33:34,000
Ehlen we sehlen bi hatina we.
 
Welcome to your arrival.

511
00:33:34,000 --> 00:33:35,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

512
00:33:35,000 --> 00:33:38,000
Welleh weza' bi xwe weza' çetine, şuxil tûneye.
 
By God, the situation itself, the situation is difficult,
there is no work.

513
00:33:38,000 --> 00:33:42,000
û dinya jî, qey dizanin, zurûfê dinyê teng biye.
 
And the world too, as you know, the world's circumstances
have become tight.

514
00:33:42,000 --> 00:33:45,000
Yanî şuxil tûneye, bi şeklê am şuxil tûneye ne.
 
Meaning there is no work, in general, there is no work.

515
00:33:45,000 --> 00:33:49,000
û mesref jî pir e. Sîtêrê avê em dikirrin, he sîtêrkê bi
şêst waraq.
 
And expenses are high. We buy water tankers, a single tanker
for sixty papers [60,000 dinars].

516
00:33:49,000 --> 00:33:52,000
Yanî deh û pênc roj, panzde roj berxwe nade.
 
Meaning ten or five days, fifteen days, it doesn't last.

517
00:33:52,000 --> 00:33:56,000
Me berê jî mehiya heştê şûnda av dikirî, noka em jî mehiya
çarê da dikirrin.
 
Before, we used to buy water after the eighth month, now we
are buying in the fourth month.

518
00:33:56,000 --> 00:33:59,000
Yanî malbetên hene, zivistanî sê av dikirrin.
 
Meaning there are families who buy water even in winter.

519
00:33:59,000 --> 00:34:01,000
Xêra baran tûnebî.
 
There was no blessing of rain.

520
00:34:01,000 --> 00:34:03,000
Sal baran ne barî, zirarê pir milet kir ne?
 
The year rain didn't fall, it harmed the people a lot,
didn't it?

521
00:34:03,000 --> 00:34:06,000
Milet pir biye, heta terbîzê erdî se tûneye.
 
The people [suffered] a lot, there isn't even ground
water/moisture.

522
00:34:06,000 --> 00:34:09,000
Yanî bide darê zeytûnê hişk bibînin, î noke.
 
Meaning, look at the olive tree, seeing it dry, right now.

523
00:34:09,000 --> 00:34:10,000
û çetine derbaz dibe?
 
And it passes with difficulty?

524
00:34:10,000 --> 00:34:12,000
Çetine derbaz dibe û zurûf me'îşet çetine.
 
It passes with difficulty and living conditions are
difficult.

525
00:34:12,000 --> 00:34:15,000
Mibalexê daye karebê nîzamî gîştî cem we?
 
Did they give the amount/supply of general national
electricity to you?

526
00:34:15,000 --> 00:34:19,000
Ê kareba heye. Kareba pir mal hene ko birîne, noka nabirin,
pir ko nabirin.
 
Yes, there is electricity. Many houses have cut it [the
national line due to cost], now they don't cut it, many
don't cut it.

527
00:34:19,000 --> 00:34:21,000
Hesebe îmkaniyata.
 
Depending on the possibilities/finances.

528
00:34:21,000 --> 00:34:22,000
Êgê nebirî, çû kerabê te...
 
If they didn't cut it, how is your electricity...

529
00:34:22,000 --> 00:34:26,000
Ne birin, de lewhaq dela û hewa xan, ser taqa şemsî xwedara
dikin.
 
If they didn't cut it, they put panels and things, they
manage themselves on solar energy.

530
00:34:26,000 --> 00:34:28,000
Xwedara.
 
Self-management.

531
00:34:28,000 --> 00:34:29,000
Ê din jî karebê nîzamî bî.
 
And the others [relied] on national electricity.

532
00:34:29,000 --> 00:34:31,000
Karebê nîzamî dibirin.
 
They cut [use] national electricity.

533
00:34:31,000 --> 00:34:35,000
û dîsa jî ta... heftê roj şanda tê dinyê.
 
And again until... seventy days passed in the world [since
it was good/available].

534
00:34:35,000 --> 00:34:36,000
Hene kareba bi xwe buha ye.
 
Some electricity itself is expensive.

535
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:42,000
Îj barê bi ro yek li ser taqê şanda bidim, ê barê jî... li
ser awê, karebê di şuxilin.
 
One load during the day I put on the [solar] panel, and the
other load... on that, on the [national] electricity they
work.

536
00:34:42,000 --> 00:34:45,000
Gundî Hecxelîl ava xwe sîtêra ji ki dikişînin tînîn?
 
The village of Hacxelil, where do they pull and bring their
tanker water from?

537
00:34:45,000 --> 00:34:47,000
Welleh berê ma jê ermîtê tîna.
 
By God, before we used to bring it from the "Armit" [likely
a local water source or name].

538
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:47,000
û noka jî biniya mala bîrek kolane, jûr nêzîk biye, esas
mifêda milet bibe, û tiştekî erzan were.
 
Aha.

539
00:34:47,000 --> 00:34:54,000
û noka jî biniya mala bîrek kolane, jûr nêzîk biye, esas
mifêda milet bibe, û tiştekî erzan were.
 
And now they dug a well below the house, the water table got
close/high, basically so the people would benefit, and it
would come somewhat cheap.

540
00:34:54,000 --> 00:34:56,000
Ê dî wekê berê ye. Me tu fêde jê nedî.
 
But it's just like before. We saw no benefit from it.

541
00:34:56,000 --> 00:35:00,000
De hele baqalim noka î bîre kî el vira... a îna çêdikolin.
 
So let's see, now this well here... they are digging these.

542
00:35:00,000 --> 00:35:05,000
De şol em fêdê av derkeve, em fêde jê bibînin. İnşallah.
 
The hope is that useful water comes out, that we benefit
from it. God willing.

543
00:35:05,000 --> 00:35:06,000
Milet fêde jê bibîne.
 
[So] the people benefit from it.

544
00:35:06,000 --> 00:35:08,000
Ê bîrê da avê belo dikê dur Hecxelîl tûne ne?
 
In the well, isn't there free water around Hacxelil?

545
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:10,000
Tûne, na. Tûne.
 
None, no. None.

546
00:35:10,000 --> 00:35:14,000
Ermîta ye û biniya mala me acer da soliya kolane.
 
It's "Armit", and below our house they dug one just
recently.

547
00:35:14,000 --> 00:35:16,000
Sîtêrê avê heta bi virginê bi çi qoyî ye ew dibînîn?
 
The water tanker, up to filling it, for how much do they
bring it?

548
00:35:16,000 --> 00:35:18,000
Welleh bi şêst waraq digihîne viro.
 
By God, for sixty papers [60,000] it reaches here.

549
00:35:18,000 --> 00:35:19,000
Sîtêr?
 
A tanker?

550
00:35:19,000 --> 00:35:21,000
Ah. Şêstî û pênc şêstî.
 
Yeah. Sixty and sixty-five.

551
00:35:21,000 --> 00:35:22,000
Ê welle buha ye.
 
Yes, by God, it is expensive.

552
00:35:22,000 --> 00:35:24,000
Î buha ye, em bê çin. Em çûkin.
 
It is expensive, where can we go? We are stuck/small.

553
00:35:24,000 --> 00:35:29,000
Sîtêr jî na pir e, teqî bîst û pênc bermîl e, bîst û heft
bermîl e, sî bermîl e, he weşte, sîtêr.
 
The tanker isn't big either, roughly twenty-five barrels,
twenty-seven barrels, thirty barrels, that's it, a tanker.

554
00:35:29,000 --> 00:35:33,000
Cema gund ê ma'zîm bi dist pêncî bardin be'dîna.
 
The people of the village... [unclear]... send fifty loads
afterwards? [Dialect unclear, possibly implying people order
a lot].

555
00:35:33,000 --> 00:35:35,000
Ê ma cema hunikîni welle.
 
Yes, well, the group handles it, by God.

556
00:35:35,000 --> 00:35:36,000
Tu zilmetî l'vê derê pir e.
 
You are a man of this place, very much so.

557
00:35:36,000 --> 00:35:37,000
Dûr wa heşke.
 
You love the surroundings.

558
00:35:37,000 --> 00:35:42,000
Heşke, dûr ma heşke wa. Erdh heşk, ezmanî dûr.
 
Love it, I love the surroundings. Dry earth, far sky.

559
00:35:42,000 --> 00:35:47,000
Xwedê ji te razî be. İnşallah, ekî dibên Xwedê rizqê milet
gî bişîne milet tûnekiya.
 
May God be pleased with you. God willing, as they say, God
sends sustenance to all the people, the people are in need.

560
00:35:47,000 --> 00:35:48,000
Amin yarab, amin. Amin.
 
Amen Oh Lord, amen. Amen.

561
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:51,000
û heya çetine derbaz dibe, bê germê noha jî zirarê bi çibike
zeytûna jî.
 
And life passes with difficulty, without the heat now
harming the olives too.

562
00:35:51,000 --> 00:35:55,000
Lê, zeytûna dike, gîtî ştî dike. Bîstiya hîn dike, bi gît
tiştî dike yanî.
 
Yes, it affects the olives, it affects everything. It
affects the orchards, it affects everything, meaning.

563
00:35:55,000 --> 00:35:58,000
Noha mîsîme qorikê l'ber pîvazê qorik ra dikin...
 
Now I hear they remove the Adam's apple [goiter] like an
onion, remove the throat [lump]...

564
00:35:58,000 --> 00:35:59,000
Dikin tiran.
 
They make them split/burst.

565
00:35:59,000 --> 00:36:03,000
Êsmok me heye, wa me dû çinî.
 
We have goiter/lumps, we picked two.

566
00:36:03,000 --> 00:36:05,000
Me dû çinî, me kir tirş.
 
We picked two, we made pickles.

567
00:36:05,000 --> 00:36:10,000
Da dû sehbab jiyan işta yek şîşeya me dane, me hemkê pê dan,
işta, em çûkin.
 
Gave two to friends, gave one bottle to us, we gave a
handful with it, well, we are stuck.

568
00:36:10,000 --> 00:36:13,000
û rêkî Heleb vebûye, rê vebûye, rêwilaq vebûne.
 
And the Aleppo road has opened, the road opened, the
pathways opened.

569
00:36:13,000 --> 00:36:14,000
Nîvan jê derm tên.
 
Half come out [swollen/bad].

570
00:36:14,000 --> 00:36:16,000
û xesta jî pir dibin.
 
And diseases are increasing too.

571
00:36:16,000 --> 00:36:20,000
Wa noka rêwilaq pir bin, xesta jî pir dibin.
 
Just as the pathways increase now, diseases also increase.

572
00:36:20,000 --> 00:36:23,000
Hinek cema hene...
 
There are some people...

573
00:36:23,000 --> 00:36:26,000
Dibe rêkî heleb jî merabe bî?
 
Could it be the Aleppo road is also blocked/bad?

574
00:36:26,000 --> 00:36:28,000
Di belo tser me.
 
It's free on us.

575
00:36:28,000 --> 00:36:33,000
No, no ne belo, ne işte mesref jî dibe.
 
No, no, not free, no well, there are expenses too.

576
00:36:33,000 --> 00:36:36,000
Dibe bî 'îdal me herimî.
 
Maybe we have become forbidden by justice.

577
00:36:36,000 --> 00:36:37,000
Ne 'eyb e.
 
Not a shame.

578
00:36:37,000 --> 00:36:39,000
Em çûk işte.
 
We are small/stuck, well.

579
00:36:39,000 --> 00:36:41,000
Soy a me.
 
Our lineage.

580
00:36:41,000 --> 00:36:42,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

581
00:36:42,000 --> 00:36:45,000
Ehlen we sehlen bi hatina we, û pir kêfxweş bûn bi hatina
we.
 
Welcome to your arrival, and we were very happy with your
arrival.

582
00:36:45,000 --> 00:36:47,000
Ma çikê mesxere jî kirin, Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
We made a little mockery/joke too, may God be pleased with
you.

583
00:36:47,000 --> 00:36:51,000
Ehlen we sehlen. De qusûrê sa me ke, ma mesxere dikir, dik
dik, çetine hene ko were, der were, bes min qusûrê sa nekir.
 
Welcome. Do not blame us, we were joking, doing this and
that, it's hard for some to come, to come out, but I didn't
blame [you].

584
00:36:51,000 --> 00:36:52,000
Hewê lextene zeqitkom.
 
[Unclear phrase - possibly "The talk hasn't stuck to you"].

585
00:36:52,000 --> 00:36:53,000
Dibe.
 
Maybe.

586
00:36:53,000 --> 00:36:55,000
Xwedê ji te razî be, em pir kêfxweş bîn.
 
May God be pleased with you, we were very happy.

587
00:36:55,000 --> 00:36:56,000
Ehlen we sehlen.
 
Welcome.

588
00:36:56,000 --> 00:37:01,000
Şîniya Hecxelîl, sehra û dinê, germê, gîd hewş û danê, gîd
malê xwe yet, hinek jî di karê xwe ne.
 
The greenery of Hacxelil, the wilderness and world, the
heat, all the yards and grain, all coming to their homes,
some are at their work.

589
00:37:01,000 --> 00:37:05,000
Bes heta em kênin, em sekin kî derkeve semêj xorê derxin,
xwedê we seferqanetin.
 
But until we laugh [enjoy], we look to see who comes out to
bring out the food/prayer rug, may God grant you
travel/contentment.

590
00:37:05,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Ehlen we sehlen, ser serê me.
 
Welcome, upon our heads.

591
00:37:06,000 --> 00:37:08,000
Temir Tat gotin te le me hene.
 
Temir Tat said you have [a debt/issue] with us.

592
00:37:08,000 --> 00:37:09,000
Welleh seheta we xweş.
 
By God, health to you.

593
00:37:09,000 --> 00:37:11,000
û serkeftin ji we ra.
 
And success to you.

594
00:37:11,000 --> 00:37:12,000
Silavê kî ti silavkê?
 
A greeting, who will you greet?

595
00:37:12,000 --> 00:37:13,000
Silavê me ji gihara hene.
 
We have greetings from the others/neighbors.

596
00:37:13,000 --> 00:37:15,000
Dûr nêzîk ji giştka ra, silavê me.
 
Far and near, to everyone, our greetings.

597
00:37:15,000 --> 00:37:16,000
Xwedê ji te razî be.
 
May God be pleased with you.

598
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:36,000
[Instrumental Music]
 
[Instrumental Music]

599
00:41:49,000 --> 00:41:53,000
Miletê kîbar, delal... saeta we xweş, bimînin bi me ra heta
dawiya vîdyoyê.
 
Noble, dear nation... have a good time, stay with us until
the end of the video.

600
00:41:53,000 --> 00:41:57,000
Qisûr nemezenin, hinekî dengê ba têt... û hewa, maşallah
dinê jî germ e.
 
Don't blame us, a bit of wind sound is coming... and the
weather, mashallah the world is hot too.

601
00:41:57,000 --> 00:42:00,000
Heta gundekî dî, derketina me... cîbicî daxwaz...
 
Until another village, our outing... fulfilling the
request...

602
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:03,000
Ev Hecî Xelîl, me piçikê wera gundî teswîr kir.
 
This is Hecî Xelîl, we filmed a little bit of the village
for you.

603
00:42:03,000 --> 00:42:05,000
Saeta we xweş û li hêviya me bin bi vîdyoyekî ecêb.
 
Have a good time and wait for us with a wonderful video.

604
00:42:05,000 --> 00:42:10,000
Ez Xelîl j'gundê Baadîna, aşqanê hatim Efrîn.
 
I am Xelîl from the village of Baadîna, I came to Afrin
passionately.

